{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat to satiety.</b> The fruits will be abundant in nourishment, as was the case with the omer, which sufficed for the grown as for the child, as the Sages of blessed memory said: אוֹכֵל קִמְעָא וּמִתְבָּרֵךְ בְּמֵעָיו — he eats a morsel and is blessed in his stomach (Torat Kohanim, Bechukotai 1:7). And the produce of the sixth year will suffice also for the seventh." "<b>And you shall dwell securely upon it.</b> You will not bear the shame of famine among the nations, in that you will not need to go to their lands to purchase grain."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:57.289466821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}